CLIFF 1.1
namespace: clarion
clan: lit-drama
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN
title: "The Last Call at the Halloway - one scene"
info: "An original one-act scene. A closing repertory theatre on its final night. "
      "Odette Rill has run the stage for thirty years; Cassian Vale left the company "
      "a decade ago and has come back for the last performance. The entries are one "
      "continuous scene and must read in order: a line's rendering may depend on a "
      "line before it."
standard: "Stage directions use a terse present-tense narrative register and never the "
          "spoken register of dialogue. Keep the venue name Halloway in Latin script. "
          "Render the surname Vale as 维尔 wherever it appears. House style: one space "
          "between Han text and Latin letters or digits, fullwidth punctuation inside "
          "Han sentences, and no textbook jargon."

[scene.arrival]
context: "The empty auditorium an hour before the final performance. A single work lamp is lit."
type: description
emotion: [calm]

<open-house-lights>
source: "The house lights are dead. One work lamp burns downstage, and the dust turns slowly in its beam."
target: "观众席的灯已经熄了。台口留着一盏工作灯，尘埃在光柱里缓缓打转。"
status: final
context: "Opening stage direction of the scene; sets the empty theatre before anyone speaks."

<enter-cassian>
source: "I could find this stage in my sleep."
target: "这座舞台，我闭着眼也摸得到。"
type: dialogue
emotion: [nostalgic, calm]
status: final
context: "Cassian speaks his first line as he walks in from the wings after ten years away."

<lit-01a>
source: "You came back."
target: "你回来了。"
type: dialogue
emotion: [joyful, grateful]
status: final
context: "Odette says this when she is genuinely glad to see him; she has hoped for this for years."

<lit-01b>
source: "You came back."
target: "你还知道回来。"
type: dialogue
emotion: [angry, sad]
status: final
context: "The same words later in the scene, said as a reproach after he admits why he left."

<reply-cassian>
source: "The call board still has my name spelled wrong."
target: "通告板上我的名字还是拼错的。"
type: dialogue
emotion: [playful]
status: final
context: "Cassian deflects with a small joke about the backstage notice board."

[scene.confrontation]
context: "They circle the argument they have avoided for ten years."
type: dialogue

<motif-promise>
source: "This theatre kept its promises. People did not."
target: "这座剧场守约，人不守约。"
emotion: [serious, sad]
status: final
context: "Odette's central line. It is quoted back by Cassian later in the scene, so the wording matters beyond this entry."

<lit-02a>
source: "Wonderful. Just wonderful."
target: "太好了，真是太好了。"
emotion: [joyful]
status: final
context: "Said when the missing lighting board key is finally found; she means it."

<lit-02b>
source: "Wonderful. Just wonderful."
emotion: [angry, playful]
target: "好啊，可真是「好」得很。"
status: final
context: "The same words after the fuse blows for the second time; bitter irony, not praise."

<callback-promise>
source: "You said the theatre kept its promises."
target: "你说过，这座剧场守约。"
emotion: [serious]
status: final
context: "Cassian quotes Odette's earlier line back at her; it must read as the same line returning."

<address-early>
source: "Mr. Vale, the call is in five minutes."
target: "维尔先生，还有五分钟开演。"
emotion: [formal, polite]
status: final
context: "Early in the scene Odette keeps him at the distance of a surname and a title."

<address-late>
source: "Cassian. Please. Sit down."
target: "卡西安，坐吧。"
emotion: [calm, sad]
status: final
context: "Late in the scene the distance drops and she uses his given name for the first time."

<lit-03a>
source: "She turns the lamp toward him."
target: "她将工作灯转向他。"
type: description
emotion: [objective]
status: final
context: "A stage direction: terse narrative register, describing the action for the crew."

<lit-03b>
source: "She turns the lamp toward him."
target: "她把灯转过来照着他。"
emotion: [playful]
status: final
context: "A line of dialogue: an actor describing the blocking aloud during a run-through, in speech."

[scene.house]
context: "Practical talk about the building itself while they avoid each other's eyes."
type: dialogue
emotion: [neutral]

<roof-year>
source: "The roof has not been touched since 1974."
target: "屋顶自 1974 年以来就没修过。"
status: final
context: "Odette lists what the building needs; the year is a fact and must survive."

<lamp-count>
source: "Two 500-watt lamps, and a fuse box older than both of us."
target: "两盏 500 瓦的灯，还有一个比我俩年纪都大的保险丝盒。"
status: final
context: "Cassian counts what is still working in the grid."

<venue-name>
source: "The Halloway does not close tonight. It closes when the last person leaves."
target: "Halloway 今晚不关门。等最后一个人走了，它才关门。"
status: final
context: "The venue name is the company's mark and is used untranslated in all materials."

<board-default>
source: "Use the default setting on the board and do not touch anything else."
target: "用调音台上的默认设置，别的什么都别动。"
status: final
context: "A technical instruction to the operator about the lighting board."

<disbelief>
source: "Are you serious? Now? After everything?"
target: "你是认真的吗？现在？在这一切之后？"
emotion: [surprised, angry]
status: final
context: "Cassian reacts to her telling him the building is already sold."

[scene.monologue]
context: "Odette alone in the work light after Cassian goes to change."
type: monologue
emotion: [nostalgic]

<monologue-open>
source: "I have swept this floor more times than I have slept in my own bed. I know which board creaks under a heavy actor and which one gives way under a light one. A building learns you, if you stay long enough."
target: "这地板我扫过的次数，比我在自己床上睡过的还多。哪块板子被体重压着会响，哪块反倒是轻轻一踩就塌，我全知道。待得够久，房子就会记住你。"
status: final
context: "The first half of her monologue, alone on stage; long-form literary prose, not conversational."

<monologue-turn>
source: "And then one night the lights do not come up, and it turns out the building never learned anything at all."
target: "然后某个晚上，灯没有亮起来，才知道房子其实什么也没记住。"
status: final
context: "The turn in the monologue where the comfort collapses."

[scene.verse]
context: "The company's traditional closing couplet, spoken to the empty house at the end of a run."
type: narration
emotion: [serious, nostalgic]

<verse-01>
source: "The lamps go dark, the boards remain."
target: "灯尽，板犹在。"
status: final
context: "First line of the closing couplet; the two lines are parallel in structure and must stay parallel."

<verse-02>
source: "The players go, the play remains."
target: "人散，戏犹存。"
status: final
context: "Second line of the couplet, mirroring the first line word for word in structure."

<final-direction>
source: "She reaches up and switches off the work lamp. Darkness, and then the house door closing."
target: "她抬手关掉工作灯。一片黑暗，随后传来观众席大门关上的声音。"
type: description
emotion: [calm]
status: final
context: "The closing stage direction of the scene."
